7513	{"artifactId":"LLD-5437d6e54c9e7d48-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-5437d6e54c9e7d48-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-16T12:11:05.873Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Switching withWriteTxn, the migration runner and the first-boot write from root.transaction to root.childTransaction makes a throwing callback's writes abort while the caller still gets its own error. This covers every part of the ISSUE's fix intent: all three sites, the original error, the bounded lock-loss wait, tests after a reopen, and the corrected migration comment.","evidence":"Outside a write txn, childTransaction calls `this.transactionAsync(callback, true)` (node_modules/lmdb/write.js:939). In executeTxnCallbacks, the asChild branch runs `env.beginTxn(1); // abortable` and on a catch runs `env.abortTxn(); txnError(error, txnCallbacks, j)` (write.js:663-680). It also awaits a thenable result before it commits (:669-671), so the migration runner's async step and its version write are aborted together when the step rejects. The caller's promise rethrows `txnCallbacks.errors[txnIndex]` (:966-969). ISSUE.md:23 asks for all three sites, the original error, the lock-loss handling, tests after a reopen and the comment fix. LLD §2.1-2.3, §4 and Migration step 1 cover each of them. [files: node_modules/lmdb/write.js, docs/standalone/graph-store-write-transaction-whose-callback-E202610165437d6e5/ISSUE.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today root.transaction commits a throwing callback's writes: the plain-callback branch records the error and does not abort the shared batch txn. withWriteTxn (store.ts:886), the migration runner (migrations.ts:442-448) and the first-boot write (store.ts:607-610) all use it.","evidence":"`transaction(callback)` delegates to `this.transactionAsync(callback)` (write.js:897-902). Its plain branch is `try { let result = userTxnCallback(); ... } catch (error) { txnError(error, txnCallbacks, j); }` (write.js:683-692), and nothing in that branch calls abortTxn. store.ts:886: `store.root.transaction(() => fn(store))`. migrations.ts:442: `await store.root.transaction(async () => { await step.run(store); ... await store.meta.put(META_SCHEMA_VERSION, step.to); })`. store.ts:607: `await root.transaction(() => { writeSchemaVersion(...); provisionSharedModulesRows(store); })`. [files: node_modules/lmdb/write.js, src/db/graph/store.ts, src/db/graph/migrations.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Production code has only three root.transaction call sites, and all 52 production withWriteTxn callers pass synchronous callbacks. The narrowed synchronous-only type therefore breaks only the one async test callback (store-health.test.ts:152).","evidence":"Grep of `.transaction(` under src finds production code only at store.ts:607, store.ts:886 and migrations.ts:442. Every other hit is a test or test helper (lmdb-smoke, store-child, migration-v2-to-v3, derived-indices). Grep of withWriteTxn calls outside __tests__ gives config/store 3, todos 11, relations 10, doc-summaries 3, repos 3, ids 3, entities 4, conversations 13 and exploration-cache 2, which is 52 calls. Each one is a plain `s => {...}` or `s => fn(s)` arrow. Grep for `withWriteTxn(async` finds only src/db/graph/__tests__/store-health.test.ts:152. [files: src/db/graph/store.ts, src/db/graph/migrations.ts, src/db/graph/__tests__/store-health.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The bounded wait and lost-lock reporting in withWriteTxn stay unchanged. childTransaction, called outside a write txn, returns the same queued promise shape as transaction, so the race, confirmLockLoss and recordLocksLost('a write transaction','write-timeout-probe') keep working. The store is opened without useWritemap, so childTransaction does not throw.","evidence":"childTransaction: `if (useWritemap) throw ...; if (writeTxn) {...nested...} return this.transactionAsync(callback, true);` (write.js:904-939). This is the same transactionAsync promise that transaction returns (:902), so it rejects with the stored error (:966-969) or never settles. store.ts:888-908 races that promise against the probe timer and needs no change. store.ts:523-527 calls `open({ path, mapSize, maxDbs })` and passes no useWritemap. [files: src/db/graph/store.ts, node_modules/lmdb/write.js]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Migration steps can stay async inside one child transaction because they run inside getGraphStore's open, before any caller can obtain the store. After locks-lost, no library transaction (now including childTransaction) is called.","evidence":"getGraphStore returns `_instance` only after it is set at store.ts:641 (`_instance = store;`). That comes after the migration call at :621, and concurrent callers await `_initPromise` (:501), so no withWriteTxn can queue during a step. After locks-lost, getGraphStore throws at :499 before any transaction call, and withWriteTxn awaits getGraphStore first (:885). store-health.test.ts:84-107 counts the patched transaction and transactionSync calls. The LLD extends that count to childTransaction. [files: src/db/graph/store.ts, src/db/graph/__tests__/store-health.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion has a test that would fail without the fix. ac1 and ac2 read the rows back (in-process and after a reopen) with a stated mutation check. The current migration test asserts only the version, so the row assertions are new and would fail on root.transaction.","evidence":"migrations.test.ts:151-176 asserts the rejection (:159), `ranA` (:164), the version (:165, :175) and `applied` (:174). It never checks rows, so the LLD's added row assertions are what expose the defect. Without the fix, a row written before a throw survives (write.js:683-692), so write-txn-atomic.test.ts and the extended migration test would fail on the current code. ac3 is a preservation criterion: lock-loss-detection.test.ts is meant to stay unchanged, and the store-health childTransaction count is new. ac4 pins the library's keep/discard behaviour (write.js:683-692 vs :663-680 vs :1024-1027), so an lmdb upgrade that changes it would fail the test. [files: src/db/graph/__tests__/migrations.test.ts, node_modules/lmdb/write.js]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":6,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-16T12:11:05.873Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
